---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="Gyro Maze Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for Gyro Maze by Kroma Digital.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">App Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy for Gyro Maze</h1>
      <p>Privacy information for the Gyro Maze Android application.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated: September 8, 2026</strong></p>

      <h2>1. About Gyro Maze</h2>
      <p>Gyro Maze is an Android maze game that uses device movement to control the ball and guide it through each maze.</p>
      <p>Gyro Maze is developed and maintained by Kroma Digital.</p>

      <h2>2. Account Registration</h2>
      <p>Gyro Maze does not require users to create an account or provide a name, email address, phone number, or other account information to use the app.</p>

      <h2>3. Motion Sensor Data</h2>
      <p>Gyro Maze uses motion sensor information from the device, such as orientation or movement data, to provide its motion-controlled gameplay.</p>
      <p>This sensor information is used for gameplay and is not used to determine the user's precise geographic location.</p>

      <h2>4. Location Data</h2>
      <p>Gyro Maze does not require precise GPS location for its core gameplay.</p>
      <p>Google AdMob may process an IP address, which can be used to estimate a device's general or approximate location for advertising, analytics, security, and fraud-prevention purposes.</p>

      <h2>5. App Data and Settings</h2>
      <p>Game settings, progress, or similar application data may be stored locally on the user's device.</p>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not operate a server for collecting or storing this locally saved game data.</p>
      <p>Deleting the app or clearing its application data may remove locally stored data.</p>

      <h2>6. Advertising and Google AdMob</h2>
      <p>Gyro Maze displays advertisements using Google AdMob and the Google Mobile Ads SDK.</p>
      <p>The app uses banner, interstitial, and rewarded advertising formats.</p>
      <p>Google Mobile Ads may automatically collect or process limited technical and advertising-related information for purposes such as displaying and measuring advertisements, analytics, security, and fraud prevention. Depending on the SDK configuration, device settings, region, consent choices, and applicable requirements, this information may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate general location;</li>
        <li>user interactions with the app and advertisements, such as app launches, taps, and ad interactions;</li>
        <li>diagnostic and performance information, including crash and app-performance information;</li>
        <li>device or account identifiers, such as the Android advertising ID or app set ID, where permitted and applicable; and</li>
        <li>advertising-related information required to provide, measure, secure, and improve advertising services.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Advertising behavior and the information processed by Google may vary depending on the user's region, device settings, consent choices, age-related settings, and the configuration of Google advertising services.</p>

      <h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Gyro Maze uses or may rely on Google services including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google AdMob;</li>
        <li>Google Mobile Ads SDK; and</li>
        <li>Google Play services and Google Play distribution services.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These services may process information according to their own privacy policies and applicable settings.</p>
      <p>Google's Privacy Policy is available at:</p>
      <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></p>
      <p>Information about how Google uses information from apps that use its services is available at:</p>
      <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a></p>

      <h2>8. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not sell users' personal information.</p>
      <p>Technical and advertising-related information may be processed or shared with Google through AdMob, the Google Mobile Ads SDK, or other Google platform services where necessary to provide advertising, analytics, app distribution, security, diagnostics, fraud prevention, or related functionality.</p>

      <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>Application data stored locally by Gyro Maze generally remains on the user's device until it is deleted by the user, cleared through device settings, or removed when the app is uninstalled, depending on the Android device and operating system behavior.</p>
      <p>Information processed by Google is subject to Google's own retention practices and applicable settings.</p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>Kroma Digital takes reasonable measures to minimize unnecessary collection of information and to limit the app's use of personal information.</p>
      <p>Information transmitted by Google Mobile Ads services is protected according to Google's security practices, including encryption in transit where applicable.</p>
      <p>However, no electronic system, device, or network transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated if Gyro Maze's features, advertising, SDKs, storage, data practices, or applicable legal and platform requirements change.</p>
      <p>Any updated version will be published on this page with a revised "Last updated" date.</p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or Gyro Maze's privacy practices, please contact Kroma Digital through the Kroma Digital Contact page:</p>
      <p><a href="/contact">https://kroma-digital.pages.dev/contact</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
